                                                             <http://purl.org/gc/SinglePoint> ;
                                                    <http://example.org/hasInputFile> <http://example.org/file_caa005b-cl-atom-basischeck_inp> ;
                                                    <http://example.org/hasOutputFile> <http://example.org/file_caa005b-cl-atom-basischeck_dat> ,
                                                                                       <http://example.org/file_caa005b-cl-atom-basischeck_log> ;
                                                    rdfs:label "Single point caa005b-cl-atom-basischeck" ;
                                                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote> "isolated Cl atom, the smallest possible case; ROHF failed (needs explicit NSETO/NPAIR for the degenerate 3p5 open shell), switched to UHF" .


###  http://example.org/exp_caa005b-cl-atom-extfil-test
<http://example.org/exp_caa005b-cl-atom-extfil-test> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                              <http://purl.org/gc/MolecularComputation> ,
                                                              <http://purl.org/gc/SinglePoint> ;
                                                     <http://example.org/hasInputFile> <http://example.org/file_caa005b-cl-atom-extfil-test_inp> ;
                                                     <http://example.org/hasOutputFile> <http://example.org/file_caa005b-cl-atom-extfil-test_dat> ,
                                                                                        <http://example.org/file_caa005b-cl-atom-extfil-test_log> ;
                                                     rdfs:label "Single point caa005b-cl-atom-extfil-test" ;
                                                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote> "same isolated Cl atom via EXTFIL (external basis file) instead of BASNAM; got further (basis read correctly) but hit the identical DGEMM crash -- ruled out BASNAM specifically as the cause, and ruled out core count (crashed the same at 8 and 1 cores)" .


###  http://example.org/exp_caa005bIRC-def2svp-test
<http://example.org/exp_caa005bIRC-def2svp-test> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
