<http://example.org/exp_caa008-water-bare> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                    <http://purl.org/gc/MolecularComputation> ,
                                                    <http://purl.org/gc/VibrationalAnalysis> ;
                                           <http://example.org/hasInputFile> <http://example.org/file_caa008-water-bare_inp> ;
                                           <http://example.org/hasOutputFile> <http://example.org/file_caa008-water-bare_dat> ,
                                                                              <http://example.org/file_caa008-water-bare_log> ;
                                           <http://purl.org/gc/hasResult> <http://example.org/energies_caa008-water-bare> ,
                                                                          <http://example.org/spectrum_caa008-water-bare> ;
                                           rdfs:label "Vibrational analysis caa008-water-bare" ;
                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote> "geometry+frequency optimization of a standalone water molecule at wB97X-D/6-31G(d,p)/PCM(water), for the hydration thermodynamic cycle" .


###  http://example.org/exp_caa008-water-pcseg2
<http://example.org/exp_caa008-water-pcseg2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                      <http://purl.org/gc/MolecularComputation> ,
                                                      <http://purl.org/gc/SinglePoint> ;
                                             <http://example.org/hasInputFile> <http://example.org/file_caa008-water-pcseg2_inp> ;
                                             <http://example.org/hasOutputFile> <http://example.org/file_caa008-water-pcseg2_dat> ,
                                                                                <http://example.org/file_caa008-water-pcseg2_log> ;
                                             <http://purl.org/gc/hasResult> <http://example.org/energies_caa008-water-pcseg2> ;
                                             rdfs:label "Single point caa008-water-pcseg2" ;
                                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote> "single-point energy at wB97X-D/PCseg-2/PCM(water) for standalone water; -76.4502962836 Hartree. Combined with 6-31G(d,p) thermal data: dG_hyd = -4.44 kcal/mol (0K, elec+ZPE), -5.99 kcal/mol (dH, 298K), but +5.88 kcal/mol (dG, 298K) -- the sign flip traced to -TdS ~ +11.9 kcal/mol, almost certainly an artifact of treating standalone water as an ideal gas (overestimated translational/rotational entropy relative to true liquid-phase water). Enthalpy trusted over raw Gibbs free energy pending a proper solution-phase entropy correction; acetaldehyde calibration (planned) will test this directly" .


